n, prioritizing objects in the wrong room and the most efficient transport plan over redundant confirmations. After any invalid attempt, use "check valid actions" and confirm the correct target location instead of repeating the failed action.', 'When When a goal requires assembling a component onto a fixture and then placing it in a container, with a limited step budget and multiple sub-tasks (inflate, mount, place).: Before supporting further actions, map each goal condition to the exact remaining action needed and track the step budget; prioritize the assembly/mounting and placement steps over optional or already-satisfied sub-tasks, and flag when the remaining steps cannot cover all conditions.', 'When When a goal specifies which particular container must hold a mixed drink and which must hold a specific ingredient, and multiple similar containers are available.: Map each goal condition to its exact target container, build and pour the mixture into its designated container first, then fill the remaining container with the required ingredient, verifying every pour destination matches the goal; after any invalid action, re-check valid actions and confirm the correct target container rather than repeating leave/grasp cycles.'], 'finalizer': ['When When building a single ordered tower from scattered blocks where each block must rest on a specific other block.: Before acting, compute the full target chain and work from the bottom up: place the base block, then stack each next block onto the growing tower, only moving a block when its required support is already in final position; after any invalid action, immediately consult valid actions and choose a move that advances the chain rather than retrying or looping on checks.', 'When When relocating a fixed set of objects from a source room to a target room with limited carrying capacity and a step limit.: Maintain an explicit delivered/remaining checklist, verify positions after each drop, and only travel while carrying 